  "question": {
    "text": "Kjeldahl&#39;s method was used for the estimation of nitrogen in an organic compound. The ammonia evolved from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>55</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of the compound neutralised <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> solution. The percentage of nitrogen in the compound is (Nearest integer)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "64",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Meq of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> used by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> in the compound&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>55</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>63</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>or</p><p>Meq. of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo></math> Meq. of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>meq</mi></math>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math>&nbsp;millimoles of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>So Millimoles of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><none/><mo>'</mo><mprescripts/><none/><mo>'</mo></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p><p>Moles of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><none/><mo>'</mo><mprescripts/><none/><mo>'</mo></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>wt. of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>%</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>14</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>55</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>63</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>66</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>"
